/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 754 0 R
/ActualText (The project aims to enhance human activity recognition using sensor data through various machine learning techniques, including SVM, Simple NN, and CNN, integrated into an interactive dashboard. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 755 0 R
/ActualText (Initially, data preprocessing involves with standardizing features. PCA is then applied to reduce dimensionality, preserving essential variance. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 756 0 R
/ActualText (An SVM model with an RBF kernel is trained and evaluated using accuracy, F1 score, and confusion matrix,)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 757 0 R
/ActualText ( A Simple NN and a CNN are also developed, each with distinct architectures involving layers for input, hidden processing, activation, and dropout, followed by evaluation and visualization. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 758 0 R
/ActualText (Finally, an interactive Streamlit dashboard is prepared, enabling real-time data analysis and model prediction, providing a comprehensive tool for understanding and deploying activity recognition models )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
